hey everyone i'm abby sharp welcome to  Abby's kitchen fall is officially here  and you know a lot of you guys are  looking for some seasonal recipe  inspiration so today a partner with base  Sal who sponsored this video to share  three plant-based sides featuring my  fall BFF sweet potatoes everyone has  that food that reminds them that fall is  coming I know a lot of my fellow  millennial women would probably say  pumpkin spice latte fair I mean when I  smell that combination of artificial  pumpkin flavoring steamed milk and  coffee I want to throw my bomber jacket  on too but the fall food that I actually  look forward to most is sweet potatoes  here in Canada saying goodbye the summer  means saying goodbye to well most of  life's pleasures corn berries patio  drinks being able to leave the house  without dressing like the Michelin Man  you know but what we do get out of our  annual trade sees is sweet potatoes now  around this time of year I admittedly  eat a lot of sweet potatoes so much so  that a lot of you guys have pointed out  that my hands are orange worth it  definitely worth it but they're high in  fiber and antioxidants and naturally low  in fat plus they are gluten free dairy  free and vegan they're also super easy  to whip up for a weeknight while also  being a classic staple ingredient for  all of the fall and winter holidays I  mean sweet potato casserole sign me up  honestly the only thing that's  disappointing about sweet potatoes is  their emoji which I really do not  believe embodies their greatness am i  right but let's be real the way I was  raised  sweet potatoes like all potatoes are  generally treated with some serious  buttery love fare but to keep these  recipes at vegan-friendly  I'm using base L vegan which has no  artificial preservatives colors or  flavors is low in saturated fat and as a  source of omega-3 fatty acids it's also  completely lactose free and gluten free  so it's an easy plant-based butter swap  so good for spreading on toast and also  a must for these three sweet potato  sides let's do this first up is my mash  to pull a sweet potatoes  I place my sweet potatoes on a lined  baking sheet and prick them with a fork  then I bake for one hour at 350 degrees  until very soft I scoop out the insides  and I mix in some base elf vegan cashew  milk chipotle pepper some extra adobo  sauce and some salt to taste then I  serve the warm  tapa cilantro and enjoy next up is my  pecan pie sweet potato wedges in a bowl  I combine some melted base l vegan maple  syrup lemon juice and pumpkin pie spice  [Music]  arrange the sweet potatoes cut into  wedges on a baking sheet so that they're  not touching then I generously brush the  maple mixture onto the sweet potatoes  and bake them for about 20 minutes then  I season with a generous pinch of fleur  de sel and crushed pecans enjoy finally  my orange Chinese five-spice twice baked  potatoes  I place my potatoes on a lined baking  sheet and pierce them with a fork then I  bake them for one hour at 305 degrees  until very soft I carefully cut an  opening into the potato lengthwise but  not cut all the way through and I gently  scoop the insights out into a bowl then  I add the base L vegan orange zest and  juice some Chinese five-spice and some  salt and I mash until smooth then I pack  the mixture back into the potato skins  and transfer to the oven for another 15  minutes or so until lightly browned on  top  finally I garnish with some crushed  cashews toasted sesame seeds and  scallions  enjoy so whether you're serving these  sweet potato sides as part of your  holiday spread or you're gonna serve  them alongside some quickie tofu steaks  on a random Tuesday night  I hope these recipes have inspired some  great easy plant-based ways to get your  sweet potato fix a big thank you again  to Bay cell for sponsoring this video  if you guys love these sweet potato  recipes please give this video a thumbs  up leave me a comment below with some of  your favorite fall staple recipes  subscribe to the channel and I'll see  you next time on Abbey's kitchen bye  [Music]
 

